---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Can’t Explain handles analytics and personal information. Google Analytics 4 is used for page views."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What we collect</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Can’t Explain is a static site. We do not run accounts, comments, or a membership
      database. The hall is files in a public git repository.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID <code>{SITE.gaMeasurementId}</code>) to
      count page views. Google may set or read cookies and process IP addresses and
      device data under its own terms. See
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The tag is loaded on every public page. It is not required to read the hall. You
      can block it with a browser or extension; the pages still work.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No login, no mailing list on this domain, no comment box.</li>
      <li>Share buttons open the destination network. Those services see the click, not us.</li>
      <li>Evidence files are public captures of already-public sources.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Author:
      <a href="/about">Colin Dixon</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
